{"id":"CVE-2005-3330","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2005-10-27T04:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T23:10:08.539Z","description":"The _httpsrequest function in Snoopy 1.2, as used in products such as (1) MagpieRSS, (2) WordPress, (3) Ampache, and (4) Jinzora, allows remote attackers to execute arbitrary commands via shell metacharacters in an HTTPS URL to an SSL protected web page, which is not properly handled by the fetch function.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://exchange.xforce.ibmcloud.com/vulnerabilities/22874","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_XF"],"name":"snoopy-httpsrequest-command-injection(22874)"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/17887","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"17887"},{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=113028858316430&w=2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20051025 SEC-Consult SA 20051025-0 :: Snoopy Remote Code Execution Vulnerability"},{"url":"https://svn.ampache.org/branches/3.3.1/docs/CHANGELOG","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/17455","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"17455"},{"url":"http://www.osvdb.org/20316","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_OSVDB"],"name":"20316"},{"url":"http://securityreason.com/securityalert/117","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SREASON"],"name":"117"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/15213","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"15213"},{"url":"http://sourceforge.net/project/shownotes.php?release_id=375385","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://securitytracker.com/id?1015104","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1015104"},{"url":"http://marc.info/?l=bugtraq&m=113062897231412&w=2","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20051027 Re: [Full-disclosure] SEC-Consult SA 20051025-0 :: Snoopy Remote"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2005/2727","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2005-2727"},{"url":"http://sourceforge.net/project/shownotes.php?release_id=368750","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2005/2335","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2005-2335"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/17330","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"17330"},{"url":"http://secunia.com/advisories/17779","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SECUNIA"],"name":"17779"},{"url":"http://www.vupen.com/english/advisories/2005/2202","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_VUPEN"],"name":"ADV-2005-2202"}],"exploitdb":[{"edb":"26424","title":"Snoopy 0.9x/1.0/1.2 - Arbitrary Command Execution","type":"remote","platform":"windows","date":"2005-10-26","verified":"1"}],"vendors":["wordpress"]}
{"id":"CVE-2005-4463","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"mitre","published":"2005-12-21T22:00:00.000Z","updated":"2024-08-07T23:46:05.507Z","description":"WordPress before 1.5.2 allows remote attackers to obtain sensitive information via a direct request to (1) wp-includes/vars.php, (2) wp-content/plugins/hello.php, (3) wp-admin/upgrade-functions.php, (4) wp-admin/edit-form.php, (5) wp-settings.php, and (6) wp-admin/edit-form-comment.php, which leaks the path in an error message related to undefined functions or failed includes.  NOTE: the wp-admin/menu-header.php vector is already covered by CVE-2005-2110. NOTE: the vars.php, edit-form.php, wp-settings.php, and edit-form-comment.php vectors were also reported to affect WordPress 2.0.1.","cwe":["n/a"],"metrics":[],"affected":[{"vendor":"n/a","product":"n/a","versions":["affected n/a"]}],"references":[{"url":"http://echo.or.id/adv/adv24-theday-2005.txt","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://NeoSecurityTeam.net/advisories/Advisory-17.txt","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/426304/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20060227 WordPress 2.0.1 Multiple Vulnerabilities"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/419999/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20051220 [ECHO_ADV_24$2005] Full path disclosure on WordPress < 1.5.2"},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/archive/1/419994/100/0/threaded","tags":["mailing-list","x_refsource_BUGTRAQ"],"name":"20051221 [ECHO_ADV_24$2005] Full path disclosure on WordPress < 1.5.2"},{"url":"http://securityreason.com/securityalert/286","tags":["third-party-advisory","x_refsource_SREASON"],"name":"286"}],"vendors":["wordpress"]}
